# D2 Icon Classes - Comprehensive Infrastructure Library
# ======================================================
#
# This file provides 100+ icon classes for infrastructure and architecture diagrams.
# Import at the top of your D2 file: ...@icons.d2
#
# TECHNOLOGY MAPPING (use this to pick the right class):
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MySQL, PostgreSQL, Aurora, MariaDB → aws-rds, gcp-sql, database
# Redis, Valkey, Memcached, ElastiCache → aws-elasticache, cache, redis
# DynamoDB, Cassandra, ScyllaDB → aws-dynamodb
# MongoDB, DocumentDB → mongodb, database
# Elasticsearch, OpenSearch → elasticsearch
# S3, GCS, Blob Storage → aws-s3, gcp-storage, azure-blob
# Kafka, MSK, Kinesis → kafka, aws-kinesis, queue
# RabbitMQ, SQS, Pub/Sub → rabbitmq, aws-sqs, queue
# Docker containers → container, docker
# Kubernetes pods/services → k8s-pod, k8s-service
# Lambda, Cloud Functions → aws-lambda, gcp-functions
# EC2, Compute Engine, VMs → aws-ec2, gcp-compute, server
# Load Balancers → aws-alb, loadbalancer
# CDN, CloudFront → aws-cloudfront, gcp-cdn
# API Gateway → aws-api-gateway, api
# External services → cloud
# Users/clients → user, users
# Go applications → golang
# Python applications → python
# Node.js applications → nodejs
# Java applications → java
#
# HOW TO USE:
# 1. Import: ...@icons.d2 (MUST be first line of your D2 file)
# 2. Apply: mynode: Label {class: aws-rds}
# 3. Render: d2 --bundle diagram.d2 output.svg
#
# TIPS:
# - Use single-line labels to avoid icon/text overlap
# - Use --bundle flag to embed icons (avoids CORS issues)
# - Classes provide both icons AND appropriate shapes/colors

